 "title": "Dark Detuned Lead",
 "category": "80s and synth-pop leads",
 "text": "Sound: a moody, hollow, slightly sour lead of dark 80s synth-pop: two square waves just out of tune with each other, gliding between notes, in a wash of chorus and echo.\n\nHow it's built: two oscillators' PULSE outputs (squares, at 50 %), one tuned a little flat; the pitch goes through a Slew first, so notes glide into each other; a mellow Ladder filter; Chorus, then a Delay. One voice: play legato for the glides.\n\nPlay: slow, minor-key melodies, legato.\n\nTweak: the second oscillator's TUNE (more is sourer), the Slew's RISE and FALL (the glide), the filter's CUTOFF, the chorus MODE.",
